{%- doc -%}
  Emits the global product-card style layer for the "BMP: Product cards"
  theme-settings panel (Plans 1+2: Card wrapper, Media, Title, Price, Swatches). Rendered once per page inside
  a <style> tag by snippets/bmp-globals.liquid, AFTER the bmp-styles.css link.

  Two kinds of output, matching the property classes documented in the
  "GLOBAL CARD STYLE" section of assets/bmp-styles.css:

  1. :root tokens (--bmp-cardg-*) — consumed by the STATIC LAYOUT rules
     in bmp-styles.css (width / align / align-flex, always emitted;
     background and radius ONLY inside the background guard; the four
     paddings of each group ONLY inside that group's *_pad_enable guard
     since 2026-08-17 — every guarded consumer carries a var() fallback,
     0px for the paddings).

  2. Token-gated RULES for font / size / line-height / letter-spacing /
     color / case / weight — properties whose baseline comes from
     per-instance preset classes (.paragraph, .h6, ...). No static
     fallback can reproduce a preset value, and an `inherit` fallback
     stomps preset rules on the element and .compare-at-price /
     .unit-price on descendants (caught in code review).
     So the rule is only emitted when the merchant set the global: at
     "Default" the rule does not exist and the render is untouched by
     construction.

     Each rule targets the element AND its direct child (`> *`), never
     ` *`. The child half is load-bearing (2026-08-14 review, thread 11):
     Horizon declares these very properties on the direct child for every
     preset except `rte` — `.paragraph > *` (base.css:669),
     `.text-block.h6 > *` (:810), `.custom-typography > *` (:1396),
     `.custom-font-size > *` (:1422) — and a child that declares a
     property never inherits the parent's. Without the child selector all
     SIX activated price blocks (3 `h6` + 3 `paragraph`) and three of the
     six title blocks (2 `paragraph` + 1 `custom`) ignored every
     typography global; only the three `rte` titles worked, which is the
     preset the original verification happened to test. (Counts are for
     the tree AFTER the cart pair was de-activated earlier in this same
     round; they read 7 and 4-of-7 before that.)
     Stopping at `> *` is equally load-bearing: .compare-at-price and
     .unit-price live two levels down, inside `<div ref=priceContainer>`,
     and must keep inheriting exactly as they do for block-level settings.
     A descendant ` *` would flatten them — the regression an earlier
     review round already caught.
     <product-price> has FOUR direct children, and `> *` reaches all of
     them (snippets/price.liquid:84 priceContainer, :135
     <small class="volume-pricing-note">; blocks/price.liquid:75 .tax-note,
     :91 .installments). Per element, what protects it:
       - priceContainer  — nothing; it is the intended target.
       - .tax-note       — `.tax-note.tax-note.tax-note` (0,3,0),
                           base.css:1313. Beats (0,2,1) for the three
                           properties it declares (font-size, font-weight,
                           color); the global still governs the rest.
       - .installments   — nothing; it follows the global. Intended.
       - .volume-pricing-note — `product-price .volume-pricing-note` is only
                           (0,1,1) (base.css:1327) and LOSES to (0,2,1), so
                           it is excluded by name below. Its h1-h6 sibling
                           rule is (0,3,1) and would have saved it, but only
                           on heading presets; three of the six activated
                           price blocks are `paragraph`. Caught in the
                           2026-08-14 audit of this very round — the earlier
                           version of this comment called the note "deeper",
                           which is what let it through.
     The PRICE selectors repeat the class on purpose.
     `product-price.bmp-card-global-price > *` is (0,1,1) and LOSES to
     `.text-block.h6 > *` (0,2,0). The ELEMENT half reaches (0,2,1) by
     doubling the class — <product-price> carries the preset class itself,
     so `.h6.h6` (0,2,0) and `.paragraph:not(.button)` (0,2,0) match it
     directly. The CHILD half gets there a different way, via the
     `:not(.volume-pricing-note)` carve-out: 1 type + 1 class + the
     :not() argument's class is also (0,2,1). Doubling the class AND
     keeping the :not() would be (0,3,1), which would newly beat
     `.tax-note.tax-note.tax-note` (0,3,0) and break the tax note instead.

     Case and weight joined class 2 on 2026-08-14. They used to be static
     rules whose var() fallback chained onto the always-on --bmp-card-*
     tokens; those are declared at bare :root while every always-on
     consumer is .product-card-scoped, so the fallback imported the card
     look into any block toggled ON outside a card. A8 now forbids them in
     the static section and A14 forbids that fallback on any unscoped
     global selector.

  These are GLOBAL settings (one state per page) — this is the layer's sanctioned
  token-gated global-rules exception, not the forbidden
  per-instance style block.
  Naming: --bmp-cardg-*, NOT --bmp-card-* — those older hardcoded tokens
  drive always-on rules and must not become settings-driven.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  echo ':root{'
  echo '--bmp-cardg-title-width:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_width | append: ';'
  echo '--bmp-cardg-title-align:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_align | append: ';'
  comment
    Second, flex-valued form of the same setting. text_alignment yields
    left/center/right; align-self / align-items need flex-start/center/flex-end.
    Both forms are consumed: the text form by the child rule (text-align), the
    flex form by the box rule (align-self, which places the whole block in the
    card column). Overriding Horizon's own --horizontal-alignment instead would
    NOT work: snippets/text.liquid derives --text-align-default from
    [style*='--horizontal-alignment: ...'], an attribute-substring match on an
    ancestor's INLINE style that no stylesheet rule can satisfy.
  endcomment
  assign bmp_title_align_flex = 'flex-start'
  if settings.bmp_card_title_align == 'center'
    assign bmp_title_align_flex = 'center'
  elsif settings.bmp_card_title_align == 'right'
    assign bmp_title_align_flex = 'flex-end'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-title-align-flex:' | append: bmp_title_align_flex | append: ';'
  comment
    max-width. `none` is deliberately emitted as the literal 100% rather than a
    --max-width--body-none token: no such token exists, and stock relies on the
    var() going invalid so text.liquid's own `min(100%, var(--max-width, 100%))`
    falls back to 100%. Pinned to the `body` family on purpose — text.liquid
    picks body/heading/display from the per-block font_size (:16-24), which a
    global cannot see. The pin is EXACT for the body and heading families at
    `normal` (both 32.5em); it differs at heading-`narrow` (19.5em vs body's
    22.75em) and differs a lot for the DISPLAY family (13em / 9.75em,
    theme-styles-variables.liquid:203-204), which a block reaches by storing a
    local font_size >= 3rem. All six shipped activations store font_size 1rem,
    so every one is body today and the pin is exact; a display-family card
    title would have its measure widened to 32.5em. Recorded rather than
    worked around — a global genuinely cannot see the per-block size.
  endcomment
  assign bmp_title_max_width = 'var(--max-width--body-normal)'
  if settings.bmp_card_title_max_width == 'narrow'
    assign bmp_title_max_width = 'var(--max-width--body-narrow)'
  elsif settings.bmp_card_title_max_width == 'none'
    assign bmp_title_max_width = '100%'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-title-max-width:' | append: bmp_title_max_width | append: ';'
  if settings.bmp_card_title_font != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-font:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_font | append: ';'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_size != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-size:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_size | append: ';'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_size_mobile != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-size-mobile:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_size_mobile | append: ';'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_weight != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-weight:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_weight | append: ';'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_line_height != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-line-height:var(--line-height--body-' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_line_height | append: ');'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_letter_spacing != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-letter-spacing:var(--letter-spacing--body-' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_letter_spacing | append: ');'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_case != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-case:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_case | append: ';'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_color != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-color:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_color | append: ';'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_background and settings.bmp_card_title_background_color != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-bg:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_background_color | append: ';'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-radius:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_corner_radius | append: 'px;'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_pad_enable
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-pad-top:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_pad_top | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-pad-bottom:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_pad_bottom | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-pad-left:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_pad_left | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-title-pad-right:' | append: settings.bmp_card_title_pad_right | append: 'px;'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-price-width:' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_width | append: ';'
  echo '--bmp-cardg-price-align:' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_align | append: ';'
  assign bmp_price_align_flex = 'flex-start'
  if settings.bmp_card_price_align == 'center'
    assign bmp_price_align_flex = 'center'
  elsif settings.bmp_card_price_align == 'right'
    assign bmp_price_align_flex = 'flex-end'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-price-align-flex:' | append: bmp_price_align_flex | append: ';'
  if settings.bmp_card_price_font != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-price-font:' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_font | append: ';'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_size != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-price-size:' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_size | append: ';'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_weight != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-price-weight:' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_weight | append: ';'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_line_height != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-price-line-height:var(--line-height--body-' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_line_height | append: ');'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_letter_spacing != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-price-letter-spacing:var(--letter-spacing--body-' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_letter_spacing | append: ');'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_case != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-price-case:' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_case | append: ';'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_color != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-price-color:' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_color | append: ';'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_pad_enable
    echo '--bmp-cardg-price-pad-top:' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_pad_top | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-price-pad-bottom:' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_pad_bottom | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-price-pad-left:' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_pad_left | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-price-pad-right:' | append: settings.bmp_card_price_pad_right | append: 'px;'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-card-gap:' | append: settings.bmp_card_gap | append: 'px;'
  if settings.bmp_card_background_color != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-card-bg:' | append: settings.bmp_card_background_color | append: ';'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-card-border-style:' | append: settings.bmp_card_border | append: ';'
  echo '--bmp-cardg-card-border-width:' | append: settings.bmp_card_border_width | append: 'px;'
  assign bmp_card_border_alpha = settings.bmp_card_border_opacity | divided_by: 100.0
  echo '--bmp-cardg-card-border-opacity:' | append: bmp_card_border_alpha | append: ';'
  if settings.bmp_card_border_color != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-card-border-color:' | append: settings.bmp_card_border_color | append: ';'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-card-border-radius:' | append: settings.bmp_card_border_radius | append: 'px;'
  if settings.bmp_card_pad_enable
    echo '--bmp-cardg-card-pad-top:' | append: settings.bmp_card_pad_top | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-card-pad-bottom:' | append: settings.bmp_card_pad_bottom | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-card-pad-left:' | append: settings.bmp_card_pad_left | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-card-pad-right:' | append: settings.bmp_card_pad_right | append: 'px;'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-media-border-style:' | append: settings.bmp_card_media_border | append: ';'
  echo '--bmp-cardg-media-border-width:' | append: settings.bmp_card_media_border_width | append: 'px;'
  assign bmp_media_border_alpha = settings.bmp_card_media_border_opacity | divided_by: 100.0
  echo '--bmp-cardg-media-border-opacity:' | append: bmp_media_border_alpha | append: ';'
  if settings.bmp_card_media_border_color != blank
    echo '--bmp-cardg-media-border-color:' | append: settings.bmp_card_media_border_color | append: ';'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-media-border-radius:' | append: settings.bmp_card_media_border_radius | append: 'px;'
  if settings.bmp_card_media_pad_enable
    echo '--bmp-cardg-media-pad-top:' | append: settings.bmp_card_media_pad_top | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-media-pad-bottom:' | append: settings.bmp_card_media_pad_bottom | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-media-pad-left:' | append: settings.bmp_card_media_pad_left | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-media-pad-right:' | append: settings.bmp_card_media_pad_right | append: 'px;'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-sw-align:' | append: settings.bmp_card_swatches_align | append: ';'
  echo '--bmp-cardg-sw-align-mobile:' | append: settings.bmp_card_swatches_align_mobile | append: ';'
  assign bmp_sw_align_logical = 'center'
  if settings.bmp_card_swatches_align == 'flex-start'
    assign bmp_sw_align_logical = 'start'
  elsif settings.bmp_card_swatches_align == 'flex-end'
    assign bmp_sw_align_logical = 'end'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-sw-align-logical:' | append: bmp_sw_align_logical | append: ';'
  assign bmp_sw_align_logical_mobile = 'center'
  if settings.bmp_card_swatches_align_mobile == 'flex-start'
    assign bmp_sw_align_logical_mobile = 'start'
  elsif settings.bmp_card_swatches_align_mobile == 'flex-end'
    assign bmp_sw_align_logical_mobile = 'end'
  endif
  echo '--bmp-cardg-sw-align-logical-mobile:' | append: bmp_sw_align_logical_mobile | append: ';'
  if settings.bmp_card_swatches_pad_enable
    echo '--bmp-cardg-sw-pad-top:' | append: settings.bmp_card_swatches_pad_top | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-sw-pad-bottom:' | append: settings.bmp_card_swatches_pad_bottom | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-sw-pad-left:' | append: settings.bmp_card_swatches_pad_left | append: 'px;'
    echo '--bmp-cardg-sw-pad-right:' | append: settings.bmp_card_swatches_pad_right | append: 'px;'
  endif
  echo '}'
  comment
    Case and weight are token-gated too, since 2026-08-14. They used to be
    static rules carrying a var() fallback onto the always-on card baseline
    (--bmp-card-title-transform / --bmp-card-title-weight /
    --bmp-card-price-weight). Those baseline tokens are declared at bare :root
    while every rule that consumes them is scoped under .product-card — but
    these global selectors are NOT, by design decision 6 (an ON toggle acts
    wherever the block renders). So a block toggled ON outside a card took
    uppercase/600 with every global still at "Default". Gating removes the
    fallback entirely: at "Default" no rule exists and nothing is imposed
    anywhere, while inside a card the always-on baseline still applies.
    Rank: (0,2,1) title / (0,1,1) price — exact ties with the always-on rules
    they must beat, won by SOURCE ORDER. That is load-bearing:
    snippets/bmp-globals.liquid renders this snippet after the bmp-styles.css
    link. Do not move the render earlier.
  endcomment
  if settings.bmp_card_title_case != blank
    echo 'div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block,div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block > *{text-transform:var(--bmp-cardg-title-case);}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_weight != blank
    echo 'div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block,div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block > *{font-weight:var(--bmp-cardg-title-weight);}'
  endif
  comment
    Price weight uses a DESCENDANT ` *`, not `> *`, unlike every other price
    rule here. It has to match the always-on baseline it overrides —
    `.product-card product-price *` — which reaches `.price` inside the
    priceContainer, two levels down. A `> *` form would leave the visible price
    at the baseline weight. Weight is the only property where this is correct:
    the baseline applies it that broadly too, so nothing is being flattened that
    was not already flat.
  endcomment
  if settings.bmp_card_price_weight != blank
    echo 'product-price.bmp-card-global-price.bmp-card-global-price,product-price.bmp-card-global-price.bmp-card-global-price *{font-weight:var(--bmp-cardg-price-weight);}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_font != blank
    echo 'div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block,div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block > *{font-family:var(--bmp-cardg-title-font);}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_size != blank
    echo 'div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block,div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block > *{font-size:var(--bmp-cardg-title-size);}'
  endif
  comment
    Per-device title size. The mobile rule is ADDITIVE and
    media-wrapped: at a blank mobile setting no rule exists and the unscoped
    desktop rule above governs every width — fallback-to-desktop by
    construction, the same shape as the hero adapt ratio. Same
    (0,2,1) selector, echoed AFTER the desktop rule, so below 750px it wins
    the tie by source order inside this very style element.
  endcomment
  if settings.bmp_card_title_size_mobile != blank
    echo '@media screen and (max-width: 749px){div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block,div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block > *{font-size:var(--bmp-cardg-title-size-mobile);}}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_line_height != blank
    echo 'div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block,div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block > *{line-height:var(--bmp-cardg-title-line-height);}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_letter_spacing != blank
    echo 'div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block,div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block > *{letter-spacing:var(--bmp-cardg-title-letter-spacing);}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_title_color != blank
    echo 'div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block,div.bmp-card-global-title .text-block > *{color:var(--bmp-cardg-title-color);}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_font != blank
    echo 'product-price.bmp-card-global-price.bmp-card-global-price,product-price.bmp-card-global-price > *:not(.volume-pricing-note){font-family:var(--bmp-cardg-price-font);}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_size != blank
    echo 'product-price.bmp-card-global-price.bmp-card-global-price,product-price.bmp-card-global-price > *:not(.volume-pricing-note){font-size:var(--bmp-cardg-price-size);}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_line_height != blank
    echo 'product-price.bmp-card-global-price.bmp-card-global-price,product-price.bmp-card-global-price > *:not(.volume-pricing-note){line-height:var(--bmp-cardg-price-line-height);}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_letter_spacing != blank
    echo 'product-price.bmp-card-global-price.bmp-card-global-price,product-price.bmp-card-global-price > *:not(.volume-pricing-note){letter-spacing:var(--bmp-cardg-price-letter-spacing);}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_color != blank
    echo 'product-price.bmp-card-global-price.bmp-card-global-price,product-price.bmp-card-global-price > *:not(.volume-pricing-note){color:var(--bmp-cardg-price-color);}'
  endif
  if settings.bmp_card_price_case != blank
    echo 'product-price.bmp-card-global-price.bmp-card-global-price,product-price.bmp-card-global-price > *:not(.volume-pricing-note){text-transform:var(--bmp-cardg-price-case);}'
  endif
-%}
